.TH "PERCH-MAIL-LIST" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-mail\-list \- list mailboxes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch mail list [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
List mailboxes on the selected IMAP server. The default output is a table; \-\-json writes one JSON object per line.
.PP
Aliases: ls.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-subscribed requires server support for LIST\-EXTENDED.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-username, \-u <value>
account username (env PERCH_IMAP_USER)
.TP
.B \-\-password <value>
account password (prefer PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD or \-\-password\-file)
.TP
.B \-\-password\-file <value>
read the account password from a file
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
read the account password from stdin
.TP
.B \-\-timeout <value>
connection timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-json
write one JSON object per mailbox
.TP
.B \-\-subscribed
only list subscribed mailboxes
.TP
.B \-\-server, \-s <value>
IMAP server (imaps://host, imap://host, or host[:port]); defaults from \-\-config
.TP
.B \-\-plaintext
connect to IMAP without TLS (use only on trusted networks)
.TP
.B \-\-starttls
require STARTTLS for IMAP
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
skip IMAP TLS certificate verification
.TP
.B \-\-ca\-file <value>
PEM CA bundle used to verify the IMAP server certificate
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch mail list \-\-server 127.0.0.1:1143 \-\-plaintext \-\-username you@example.com

perch mail list \-\-server imaps://mail.example.com \-\-username you@example.com \-\-json
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_USER
default account username
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD
account password
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\fR(1)
